{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794172767,"nonce":"cWMRMDXbMrGGKQ8REAbDS2AbRVM=","title":"L4 — Cross-repo issue list with filters and roadmap-open view","message":"## Context\nCore view: every issue from every repo, filterable. Sidebar `Section::Bugs` (`src/main.rs:12`) becomes `Issues`; the header's \"Add Filters\" (`src/ui/screen.rs:123` `content`) becomes a real filter bar.\n\n## Files\n- `src/filter.rs` — new, in lib: `Filter` + pure `matches(\u0026Issue, \u0026Filter)`\n- `src/ui/screen.rs` — Issues page, filter bar, rows\n- `src/main.rs:12` — rename the section\n\n## Approach\n- `Filter { kinds: set of Kind, status: Open | Closed | All (default Open), state: Any | InProgress | Blocked, repos, labels, text }`; text matches title and human id, case-insensitive.\n- Filter bar: kind chips, status segmented control, state, repo picker, search `text_input`; result count.\n- Row: kind chip, title, `human_id`, repo name, state badge, labels via `components::chip` (`src/ui/components.rs:68`).\n- \"Open roadmap\" preset = `/roadmap-open` semantics (`../skillforge/plugins/roadmap/README.md`, Commands table): open only, in-progress/blocked first, children nested under their epic, ordered by layer.\n\n## Depends on\nL3 — loaded issues in `App`\n\n## Out of scope\n- Detail pane (L6), actions (L7).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- `matches` unit tests cover each filter dimension and a combination\n- Unit test: the roadmap-open grouping puts in-progress/blocked first and nests children under their epic by layer\n- All three gates pass","files":null}]}